A||||5||BOILERMAKER||Vegas Trip was a Hoot!||||1||
Z||000000||BOILERMAKER||09-23-2000||09:44 AM||||Well, I'm back from Vegas and Cali.  That was an enlightening trip.  Wow, I've never seen so much dry earth at one time.  Drove over 1000 miles and saw a couple of Fiero coupes, one GT on Santa Monica Blvd in LA, and a special wrapped one (couldn't tell exactly what it was, but it looked cool) on the way back to Vegas.<P>Everyone has asked me how I made out gambling wise.  Let's just say that the leather seats will be on their way in a couple of months, but there is no near-future V8 heading my way.<P>Was hoping to see a couple more Fiero's, but I guess I wasn't looking in the right places.  Went to Bakersfield, CA via Barstow and then went down to LA from Bakersfield, and then back to Vegas and only saw a handful.<P>Now back to the hobby!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Greg Piet||09-23-2000||10:01 AM||||Well I am guessing you did not see a not so pretty red Fiero in Las Vegas with a big 47 on the doors?   Oh well   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>There are about 7 Fieros I see in Vegas on a regular basis(mine is in that count), and 3 others I see every so often.<BR>||||reg||1
